anya: quick note 1 I opened a tiny PR to consolidate streaming + pagination snippets (py/ts/go). aim: show safe close, resume token semantics, kv cache hint, and a short page-stream dedupe example. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5278 :sparkles:

leo: nice. can you include a one-line rule about resume ordering? i.e., always resume with the last resume_token seen for that stream/page.

anya: yes; added: 'Always resume using the most recent resume_token for that stream or page and pass the same kv_cache_hint.'

samir: added a compact python snippet showing context manager style + retry/resume comment. pls check naming.

samir: ```python
# python: streaming pattern (context manager)
with client.stream('gpt-4o-mini', batch_size=4, kv_cache_hint='user:abc') as s:
    try:
        s.send('analyze document:\n' + text)
        for chunk in s:
            handle(chunk)
    except TransientError:
        # persist resume_token somewhere durable, then resume using it
        s.resume(persisted_resume_token)
```

mira: small nit: add explicit finally/close example in TS to avoid leaked sockets. i'll add a TS snippet.

mira: ```ts
// typescript: ensure close() in finally
const s = await client.stream('gpt-4o-mini', { batchSize: 4, kvCacheHint: 'user:abc' })
try {
  await s.send('analyze document:\n' + text)
  for await (const chunk of s) {
    onChunk(chunk)
  }
} finally {
  await s.close()
}
```

leo: can we show a one-line explanation on batching tradeoffs? keep it short.

anya: added under "Batching guidance": "Use batch_size=3-5 for low-latency interactive streams; increase to 8+ for throughput-oriented batches."

samir: added a small Go sketch showing jittered backoff and explicit Resume(lastToken) call.

samir: ```go
// go: stream sketch with backoff + resume
s, _ := client.Stream("gpt-4o-mini", StreamOptions{BatchSize:4, KVCacheHint:"user:abc"})
defer s.Close()
for {
  chunk, err := s.Recv()
  if err == io.EOF { break }
  if err != nil {
    time.Sleep(jitteredBackoff(retries))
    // resume using last saved resume token for this stream/page
    s.Resume(lastResumeToken)
    continue
  }
  process(chunk)
}
```

anya: added a new mini-section "Paginated streams" with a short pseudo-example: persist per-page resume_token + last_seq id and dedupe on resume. kept it compact so readers can copy the pattern.

mira: LGTM. small link nit: one inline link still targets the old pagination doc. i'll push a follow-up to update after merge.\
